# tally 2.2 (CHANGES.md 2.2-10, pick P14): the fault's fix is at the trimming, and the dependency graph is tally
# 2.1.8's. A def keyed by an event kind and an ordered index, read at a shifted index with no guard by a def a
# transfer's amount reads: an edge for the def's key would make its read a guard question (LOAD-GUARD); with the graph
# unchanged it answers as tally 2.1.8's refcore does. Expect: tally 2.1.8's refcore, byte for byte.
=== m.tally
model n4
  tally 2
  on 2025-04-01
  start 2025-01-01
  end 2025-06-30
  note "N-4 probe: a def keyed by an event kind and an ordered index, read at a shifted index with no guard by a def a transfer's amount reads."

source s "s"
unit DUK: currency minor 0.01
index mon = month 2025-01..2025-06
place konto: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..
place world: outside lives 2025-01-01..
input d0: date
input f: money DUK
input mk: month

def d[t in transfers, m in mon]: money DUK = f
def r[t in transfers, m in mon]: money DUK = d[t, m - 1]

move m0: transfers
  on d0
  leg cash from world to konto amount f

move m1: transfers
  on d0
  leg cash from world to konto amount r[m0, mk]

ask q: bal(konto, 2025-06-30)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  d0 = 2025-01-05 "s"
  f = 1.00 "s"
  mk = 2025-03 "s"
  opening[konto] = 0.00 at 2025-01-01 start "s"
=== expect
q: 2.00 DUK
  unfulfilled: m0
  unfulfilled: m1
  cut 2025-04-01
